# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments; otherwise, check them in:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1255, pipenv should generally not be check into control.
#   Only in very special cases should these be committed.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains exact version definitions, which
#   is generally recommended to commit in applications but not in libraries.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains exact version definitions
# pdm.lock

